# Firebase

- Import Firebase runtime only from `src/services/**`.
- Init app in `src/services/firebase.ts`; Auth/Firestore wrappers in sibling services.
- Auth: email/password, email link (`/auth/email-link`), Google.
- Admin gate: `admins/{uid}` document exists — never client-writable.
- Clients must **not** update `courses.dates`. Use `/api/enroll` and `/api/unenroll` (Bearer ID token).
- Admin user delete must use `/api/delete-user` (Auth `deleteUser` + `users/{uid}`); clients must not delete `users` docs directly.
- Browser `/api/*` goes through Next `src/app/api/[...path]` → private Cloud Run `api` (Google ID token). Firebase Bearer is forwarded as `X-Firebase-Authorization`.
- Gen2 `api` runtime SA (`PROJECT_NUMBER-compute@developer.gserviceaccount.com`) needs `roles/datastore.user` (+ `roles/firebaseauth.admin` for Auth admin APIs). Org policy blocks public invoker.
- Admin CRUD of courses/dates/CMS uses Firestore with admin rules.
- Localhost uses the real Firebase project (Auth, Firestore, Cloud Functions) — no emulators. For local `/api` proxy, ADC must mint Cloud Run ID tokens (e.g. App Hosting compute SA impersonation).
